 ## Background
-Originated in 3D Surface Splatting (3DSS) [Ye et al. 2024b; Yu et al. 2024b], as an improvement over the densification criterion used in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) [Kerbl et al. 2023] and the approximation used in 2DGS [Huang et al. 2024]. It addresses the issue of over-reconstructed regions being incorrectly identified for refinement by using a principled criterion based on screen-space gradients [S1, unofficial].
